# src/apps/daemon/internal/networking/multipath

## Purpose
Owns multipath networking primitives that coordinate traffic across more than one eligible network path.

## Contents
Contains Go path state, scheduling/selection, health, and transport helpers used by multipath-capable flows.

## Interfaces and dependencies
Consumed by daemon networking/routing layers and depends on connection primitives, timing/health observations, and context cancellation.

## Invariants
Path selection is deterministic for equivalent state, unavailable paths are not selected as healthy, lifecycle cancellation reaches all owned work, and path/resource state is synchronized across concurrent access.